      "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\n`flatten_products` reads only `product[\"test_case\"][0]`. Both grouped inference performance recipes therefore omit their async-scheduler scenario: `gpt_583m_perf_async_sched` on H100 and `gpt_583m_perf_async_sched_gb200_4gpu` on GB200.\n\nExpand the outer test-case list as another Cartesian dimension alongside the existing parameters. Cadence stays a list-valued attribute, and legacy scope aliases retain their per-row cadence semantics.\n\nThe regressions load both existing recipe files through the production parser and also exercise multiple cases across platform/scope combinations.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Reproduced on unchanged production code: focused regressions **3 failed**.\n- After the fix, the same focused tests **3 passed** in the Linux Python 3.12 CPU tooling container.\n- `uv run --no-project --python /opt/cpu-review/bin/python isort` on both changed files; Black 26 check, isort check, Ruff, and Python compile checks passed.\n- Required `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` completed successfully with the pinned Black 26.3.0, isort 5.13.2, Pylint 3.2.6, and Ruff 0.9.10. Its nonblocking mypy step reports 18 pre-existing source errors, confirmed on unchanged baseline; no new mypy diagnostics.\n- GPU training validation is not covered by these CPU orchestration tests.\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest -q tests/test_utils/python_scripts/test_recipe_multiple_test_cases.py\n```\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: none; this is a small, reproduced bug fix, not a new feature or GPU kernel.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] Added relevant focused regressions.\n- [ ] Added GPU functional tests.\n- [x] Ran the repository formatter.\n\nAI-assisted draft; human author review and NVIDIA GPU/full CI validation are pending. The personal author-review checkbox is left unchecked.\n",
